                <pb facs="0712" n="592" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg592"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00 Revolutions/38: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-27T13:00:00-06:00">April 27, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>77. Department’s telegram number 29, April 25, 2 p.m. Honduran Government has
                    ordered munitions from Remington Arms Company, see my telegram 73, April 25,
                    noon. Understand a few riot guns are to be shipped next steamer from New Orleans
                    by another American firm. Believe the Honduran Government will not deal with
                    California Arms Company.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
